  "topic": "inlay_hints",
  "subtopic": "parameter_hints",
  "title": "Dependent calls",
  "summary": "Parameter names appear even when the callee is only known inside a template",
  "prose": "Candidates are matched by argument count and by the arguments whose type is known; only a unique surviving candidate names the parameters, so a call that could still hit several overloads stays bare rather than guessing.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "template <typename T>\nvoid apply(T scale);\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nstruct Holder {\n    void member(T item);\n    static void static_member(T slot);\n};\n\nvoid overload(int value);\nvoid overload(double value);\n\nvoid place(int x, int y);\nvoid place(const char* name, int y);\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nstruct Runner {\n    void run(Holder<T> holder, T value) {\n        apply(value);\n        holder.member(value);\n        Holder<T>::static_member(value);\n        overload(T{});\n        place(1, value);\n    }\n};\n",
